# AI/ML Development Standards

## AI Integration Best Practices

### Model Usage
- Always implement proper error handling for AI API calls
- Include timeout configurations for AI requests
- Implement retry logic with exponential backoff
- Cache AI responses when appropriate to reduce costs
- Log AI interactions for debugging and monitoring

### Prompt Engineering
- Store prompts in separate configuration files or constants
- Use structured prompts with clear instructions
- Include examples in prompts for better results
- Version control prompt templates
- Test prompts thoroughly before deployment

### Data Handling
- Validate all input data before sending to AI models
- Sanitize student submissions to prevent prompt injection
- Implement data privacy measures (anonymization when needed)
- Store original submissions separately from processed data
- Handle various file formats (PDF, DOCX, TXT, etc.)

### Grading Logic
- Implement rubric-based scoring systems
- Provide detailed feedback explanations
- Allow for manual review and grade adjustments
- Track confidence scores from AI models
- Implement bias detection and mitigation strategies

### Performance Considerations
- Batch process multiple submissions when possible
- Implement queuing for large grading jobs
- Use streaming responses for real-time feedback
- Monitor token usage and costs
- Optimize prompt length while maintaining quality